{
  "$schema": "folio-block-summaries/v1",
  "entry": "10665-44796-ara",
  "summaries": [
    {
      "block": "library/10665-44796-ara/blocks/prose-sec-000",
      "source": "sections/sec-000-اﻹﻃﺎر-اﻟﺨﺎص-ﺑﺎﻟﺘﺄﻫﺐ-ﻟﻸﻧﻔﻠﻮﻧﺰا-اﻟﺠﺎﺋﺤﺔ.md",
      "source_hash": "e086de5a150b32ba5ffdf33d18db9dc39f03452f9adc02303c3c999b926aff57",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "The cataloguing and copyright page of the Arabic edition of the Pandemic Influenza Preparedness (PIP) Framework, with ISBN, WHO copyright and standard disclaimers.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-44796-ara/blocks/prose-sec-001",
      "source": "sections/sec-001-اﳌﺤﺘـﻮﻳــﺎت.md",
      "source_hash": "b792467d593b3f34ff0a063c39bb32766a9470c274059667a04d7a8382669ed1",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "The first part of the table of contents, listing the framework's principles, objective, scope, definitions and the virus-sharing system.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-44796-ara/blocks/prose-sec-002",
      "source": "sections/sec-002-12-وﻓريوﺳﺎت-اﻷﻧﻔﻠﻮﻧﺰا-اﻷﺧﺮى-اﻟﺘﻲ-ﻗﺪ-ﺗﺴﺒﺐ-ﺟﺎﺋﺤﺔ-ﺑ.md",
      "source_hash": "35ca18b939d3fe0ff0357bef322bde628c876411303a994a165d331bad82eaaa",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "The rest of the table of contents, covering the virus-sharing provisions, the benefit-sharing system, governance and the annexes, followed by the heading of World Health Assembly resolution WHA64.5 of May 2011.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-44796-ara/blocks/prose-sec-003",
      "source": "sections/sec-003-اﻟﺘﺄﻫﺐ-ﻟﻸﻧﻔﻠﻮﻧﺰا-اﻟﺠﺎﺋﺤﺔ-ﺗﺒﺎدل-ﻓريوﺳﺎت-اﻷﻧﻔﻠﻮﻧﺰا.md",
      "source_hash": "1324d20ffbbac24e04bbb4d64adca47aa83c63f040bc5055862c4b5c05c64c4c",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "World Health Assembly resolution WHA64.5, which adopts the PIP Framework, recognises industry's role and asks the Director-General to implement, monitor and report on it every two years.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-44796-ara/blocks/prose-sec-004",
      "source": "sections/sec-004-١-اﳌﺒﺎدئ.md",
      "source_hash": "deccefabeca6ab7049cd37230b02b27b1da4be1c1682f0b44af52f8be7784346",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "Sets out the principles agreed by WHO Member States, recalling earlier resolutions and noting the threat of a pandemic, especially for developing countries. It commits states to share H5N1 and other potential pandemic influenza viruses and their benefits on an equal footing, and recognises the sovereign right over biological resources, the importance of technology transfer and the need to fund access to vaccines in developing countries.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-44796-ara/blocks/prose-sec-005",
      "source": "sections/sec-005-٢-اﻟﻐﺮض.md",
      "source_hash": "ef6df9243832ad8ff18cabdb921730a165bbe8d76028aa216ac83c9f745e5e10",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "States the framework's objective of improving pandemic preparedness through a fair, transparent and equitable system for sharing H5N1 and other potential pandemic viruses and the benefits. It defines its scope as excluding seasonal influenza and non-influenza pathogens.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-44796-ara/blocks/prose-sec-006",
      "source": "sections/sec-006-٤-اﻟﺘﻌﺎرﻳﻒ-واﳌﺼﻄﻠﺤﺎت.md",
      "source_hash": "09e8ddcebfc3a3f7f47400ff716075f2f1d85556fb38adbb1dd6bacdb8b682b7",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "Defines PIP biological materials, such as clinical specimens, wild-type virus isolates and candidate vaccine viruses made by WHO network laboratories, along with other technical terms like wild-type influenza viruses and genetic sequences.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-44796-ara/blocks/prose-sec-007",
      "source": "sections/sec-007-أﺳامء-اﳌﺆﺳﺴﺎت-واﳌﻨﻈامت-واﻟﻜﻴﺎﻧﺎت.md",
      "source_hash": "0144e233d5875adc0a4ef25dd2ef92a2c5480b5cb84a2bf0f04a88186fc1158d",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "Defines the institutions and entities named in the framework, including essential regulatory laboratories, influenza vaccine, diagnostic and pharmaceutical manufacturers, national influenza centres and WHO's PIP vaccine stockpile.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-44796-ara/blocks/prose-sec-008",
      "source": "sections/sec-008-٥-ﻧﻈﺎم-اﻟﺘﺄﻫﺐ-ﻟﻸﻧﻔﻠﻮﻧﺰا-اﻟﺠﺎﺋﺤﺔ-ﻣﻦ-أﺟﻞ-ﺗﺒﺎدل-وﻓر.md",
      "source_hash": "3510d6ddcfe9b9810fbf37fbbb59736daab3eeee2a8309a22b950af0989bedbf",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "The heading for section 5 on the PIP system for sharing H5N1 and other potential pandemic influenza viruses.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-44796-ara/blocks/prose-sec-009",
      "source": "sections/sec-009-اﻷﺣﻜﺎم-اﻟﻌﺎﻣﺔ.md",
      "source_hash": "96bafaf65bacab259aa2fa3699a99192569f4f804c1429ed2c29d9f1623e029b",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "Sets out the general provisions for virus sharing, under which Member States send PIP materials from human H5N1 and other potential pandemic cases to WHO collaborating centres or H5 reference laboratories and consent to onward transfer. It also covers genetic sequence data and the traceability mechanism, noting that its terminology has been changed.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-44796-ara/blocks/prose-sec-010",
      "source": "sections/sec-010-ﺻﻴﻎ-اﻻﺗﻔﺎق-اﳌﻮﺣﺪ-ﻟﻨﻘﻞ-اﳌﻮاد.md",
      "source_hash": "12542a178e82ebe1c06490ed304c331eedb86121f3e1fd548eb9972e546dd663",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "States that Standard Material Transfer Agreement 1 covers transfers within WHO's network and SMTA 2 covers transfers outside it. It then opens section 6 on benefit sharing, setting out its general provisions, such as surveillance, risk assessment and capacity building.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-44796-ara/blocks/prose-sec-011",
      "source": "sections/sec-011-ﺗﻨﺴﻴﻖ-ﻣﻨﻈﻤﺔ-اﻟﺼﺤﺔ-اﻟﻌﺎﳌﻴﺔ-ﻟﻠﺘﺄﻫﺐ-واﻟﺘﺼﺪي-ﻟﻸﻧﻔﻠﻮﻧ.md",
      "source_hash": "2bc133e186b172470a7c59c1551987307d60f746586665d221bc3963e19a1d51",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "Describes WHO coordination of pandemic preparedness and response under the International Health Regulations (2005), with fair allocation of scarce resources. It also covers pandemic risk assessment and the supply of candidate vaccine viruses, diagnostic reagents and test kits. Laboratory and surveillance capacity building in developing countries is also addressed.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-44796-ara/blocks/prose-sec-012",
      "source": "sections/sec-012-ﺑﻨﺎء-اﻟﻘﺪرات-اﻟﺘﻨﻈﻴﻤﻴﺔ.md",
      "source_hash": "fc46c3f25799f2e9c730d7849e051d2e4b58cd5e941caeaa26675cbe4e28d43c",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "Covers regulatory capacity building for rapid approval of influenza products, national antiviral stockpiles and the WHO stockpile of PIP vaccines, including deployment plans and use in affected countries before a pandemic.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-44796-ara/blocks/prose-sec-013",
      "source": "sections/sec-013-٦٠١-إﺗﺎﺣﺔ-اﻟﻠﻘﺎﺣﺎت-ﰲ-اﻟﻔﱰة-اﻟﻔﺎﺻﻠﺔ-ﺑني-أي-ﺟﺎﺋﺤﺘن.md",
      "source_hash": "4125d4fefbe35b7987dbc900702ec1a5b83b73775992becb9eaf9bc8f85f9fc1",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "Describes measures to improve access to pandemic influenza vaccines in developing countries between and during pandemics, including reserving part of production, tiered pricing based on country income and technology transfer. It sets out the annual partnership contribution from manufacturers, benchmarked at half the estimated US$56.6 million running cost of the WHO network in 2010.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-44796-ara/blocks/prose-sec-014",
      "source": "sections/sec-014-٧-ﺗﴫﻳﻒ-اﻟﺸﺆون-واﻻﺳﺘﻌﺮاض.md",
      "source_hash": "4b61bc5d017ed1c27f900e86276e6857e0216119270ed817d8f0cdc489fbb47f",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "Sets out governance of the framework, with oversight by the World Health Assembly and an independent Advisory Group of international experts. It also describes how the Director-General reviews breaches of terms of reference or transfer agreements and may suspend or revoke a laboratory's WHO designation.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-44796-ara/blocks/prose-sec-015",
      "source": "sections/sec-015-رﺻﺪ-واﺳﺘﻌﺮاض-اﻹﻃﺎر.md",
      "source_hash": "d45df30d4de906ca4a758dc86f276b8e8485d5ee1375c90fc26287734d44f239",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "Requires the Director-General to report to the World Health Assembly every two years on laboratory capacity, vaccine production capacity, benefit sharing and contributions, and schedules a review of the framework by 2016.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-44796-ara/blocks/prose-sec-017",
      "source": "sections/sec-017-اﳌﻠﺤﻖ-١.md",
      "source_hash": "c3baeb454677fb1fa856a1f85284c5e41a319af77397a9ce3864808a8f7c7a4a",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "Annex 1, Standard Material Transfer Agreement 1 for transfers within WHO's global influenza surveillance network, setting out the parties, the materials covered and obligations such as involving and acknowledging scientists from originating countries.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-44796-ara/blocks/prose-sec-018",
      "source": "sections/sec-018-اﳌﺎدة-٦-ﺣﻘﻮق-اﳌﻠﻜﻴﺔ-اﻟﻔﻜﺮﻳﺔ.md",
      "source_hash": "503ccdd2d75553198c74b7826442c2d7401261d0781c43d22a78ae02a8f404e1",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "Articles of SMTA 1 stating that neither party may seek intellectual property rights on the materials, with terms on prior rights, dispute settlement, suspension or withdrawal and acceptance without a printed signature.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-44796-ara/blocks/prose-sec-019",
      "source": "sections/sec-019-اﳌﻠﺤﻖ-٢.md",
      "source_hash": "62dd416b133ce9a3c99874295f6ddcd303690e5af87f1a9126b02ee0f3975b01",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "Annex 2, Standard Material Transfer Agreement 2 between WHO and recipients outside its network, setting out the parties, materials and the recipient's commitments, including onward sharing only with other SMTA holders.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-44796-ara/blocks/prose-sec-020",
      "source": "sections/sec-020-اﳌﺎدة-٥-ﻓﺾ-اﻟﻨﺰاﻋﺎت.md",
      "source_hash": "b26355decbdf0d5ed8ba886f4c1717d8fbacfc0c27a697e053d0818616bf59a5",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "Further articles of SMTA 2 on dispute settlement by binding arbitration, WHO's privileges and immunities, and signature, with several terms left for the parties to agree.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-44796-ara/blocks/prose-sec-021",
      "source": "sections/sec-021-اﳌﻠﺤﻖ-٣.md",
      "source_hash": "5888b09e9c1545ad70d6888512baff3da395787922f782dfe7018470bdfbe4e5",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "Annex 3, the terms of reference of the PIP Advisory Group, setting out its functions of monitoring the framework and advising on topics such as stockpiles, surveillance, the traceability mechanism and use of contributions.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-44796-ara/blocks/prose-sec-022",
      "source": "sections/sec-022-٣-ﺗﻌﻴني-اﻷﻋﻀﺎء.md",
      "source_hash": "b6f2c0de98e93a4b5a91461f6822b61198b633e508f73b747cb04c6b026fec16",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "Describes how the 18-member Advisory Group is formed from three Member States per WHO region and how it operates, including meetings, reporting and conflicts of interest. A further section lists commitments on sharing genetic sequence data and acknowledging laboratories that supply PIP materials.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-44796-ara/blocks/prose-sec-023",
      "source": "sections/sec-023-اﳌﻠﺤﻖ-٥.md",
      "source_hash": "29f36a220e1318d0bc86e95b05a177f0e54cce5db5be28a96900bd7bfe6957da",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "Annex 5, terms of reference for WHO collaborating centres for influenza when handling PIP materials, describing the global surveillance network and their duties on sharing materials and sequence data.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-44796-ara/blocks/prose-sec-024",
      "source": "sections/sec-024-اﻻﺧﺘﺼﺎﺻﺎت-اﻷﺳﺎﺳﻴﺔ.md",
      "source_hash": "280588a1d960d4a3d24d6124b291a5f1c160a3151a8299f9ee11fcefabe6ff48",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "Sets out the core terms of reference for WHO collaborating centres for influenza, covering coordination with the WHO global influenza programme, virus characterisation, candidate vaccine development, training and support to national centres. It also requires them to acknowledge contributors in publications according to editorial guidelines.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
